From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdoupe
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:27:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/24] Keep mpv and Chromium video decode on the iGPU of
 hybrid laptops

Render nodes follow PCI order, so on some hybrids the NVIDIA GPU is
renderD128 and video decode wakes it. Pin mpv (hwdec=vaapi plus
vaapi-device) and Chromium-family browsers (--render-node-override) to
the display iGPU's by-path node, for new users, browser installs,
Chromium refreshes and existing installs. Settings the user already
has are kept, and other machines are untouched.

Backport to v4.5.0-rc1: the brave-widevine and platform-app-hooks tests build a
stub OMARCHY_PATH, so they stand in a no-op hybrid_video_pin_chromium for the
new helper; default-apps-test runs on the real tree and needs none. In
install/user/all.sh the new step follows vm-no-animations.sh; nvidia.lua keeps
the hybrid-cursor require after the stale-pin check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5
Backport-of: 44a952a3bf3e34417b2c1120ecc15c494c0e38fb
Backport-of: ed59a8b7b22e80bba000abcf55f2eca7343141b8 (fixup)
